NODE id=matrix/cody/internal/worker.loopDetector kind=type
  digest=b3:b3e728fc8a5e0cf87a54e3f77ef08a7a11eb9e3a84c6af89fed69bf1cd0b0086 file=cody/internal/worker/loop.go range=22:28 lang=go exported=false byte_range=623:949
  sig=type loopDetector struct {\n	sigs []string\n}
  doc=loopDetector is the stuck-worker guard: it hashes every (tool, input,\noutput) triple and stops the run when the identical call keeps producing\nthe identical result. A repeated call whose OUTPUT changes (e.g. polling a\nbackground job as it makes progress) never trips it.
EDGES
